    "northStar": "The Precision Instrument",
    "overview": "DecentralExchange is built like an instrument, not a dashboard template. Balances and prices are the truth of every screen, so they get the size, the weight and the motion; everything around them recedes into material. The ground is Apple's neutral grey, content sits on white (graphite in dark mode) surfaces lifted by one soft shadow, and the only chroma on a resting screen is the logo's indigo on whatever the holder is about to press or has selected. Buy and sell speak in system green and red, and nothing else is allowed to borrow them.\n\nThe craft bar is Apple Wallet and Stocks, macOS System Settings and Uniswap's swap card, played at full fidelity: large titles, grouped inset lists with hairlines that start past the avatar, segmented controls whose selection rides on a raised thumb, a translucent top bar content scrolls beneath, and digits that roll to their new value. The same system runs across the desktop shell, the mobile shell, the landing page and the auth screens, in light and dark, in 17 languages. Density is comfortable rather than terminal-like: an 8px rhythm, 44px tap targets, 24px card padding.\n\nMotion is one physical system. A single spring (stiffness 520, damping 38, mass 0.8) drives every sliding selection, sheet, toast and press, and Apple's curve `cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)` drives every tween. Presses answer with scale (0.97) and tint, never with an ink ripple. The component kit in `src/components/premium/` ports 21st.dev components into styled-components and motion; each file credits its origin.",
    "rules": [
      {
