      {
        "body": "Every six-digit hex outside the token files must appear in the policy script's palette set. A new color is a system change, not a styling choice. Crypto brand colors (Bridge, Swap, the coins marquee) are the one exemption, kept native.",
        "name": "The Sanctioned Palette Rule",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "body": "Every price, balance, amount and metric renders in tabular numerals, and every balance and price that changes rolls its digits (AnimatedNumber, 750ms on the system curve) instead of swapping text.",
        "name": "The Tabular Truth Rule",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "body": "Weights are 400, 500 and 600. 700 is permitted for rare emphasis; 100, 200, 300, 800 and 900 fail the policy check.",
        "name": "The Weight Ceiling Rule",
